VALUES ('8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 'ckad-services-networking', 'CKAD Practice: Services & Networking', 'kubernetes', ARRAY['CKAD', 'Services', 'Ingress', 'NetworkPolicy', 'DNS']::TEXT[], 37, 'standard', true, 6, 60, 1, 0);

-- ── Section: Services (13 questions) — Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum's Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material. ──

VALUES ('37a116c3-614a-480b-ae11-36ff59cdf800', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 1, 'Which Service type is the default when ''type'' is omitted from a Service spec?', 'Services & Networking', 'Service Types', 'mcq');
VALUES ('37a116c3-614a-480b-ae11-36ff59cdf800', '835879d3-d3da-4a96-b16e-05b3286113f1', 'ClusterIP is the default Service type, exposing the Service only on an internal cluster IP reachable from within the cluster.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('233fadad-2c76-4f01-9646-e4d57b66f453', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 2, 'What does a Service of type ExternalName actually do?', 'Services & Networking', 'ExternalName Service', 'mcq');
VALUES ('233fadad-2c76-4f01-9646-e4d57b66f453', '25f2f3d9-6bc1-4c7f-9248-17ebbe825d81', 'ExternalName Services work purely at the DNS level, returning a CNAME to spec.externalName. There''s no selector, no Endpoints, and no actual traffic proxying by kube-proxy.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('a5b1e851-27ea-4379-96d1-816715fa042d', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 3, 'A Service is created with no ''selector'' field. As an application developer, when is this pattern useful, and what do you have to do to make it work?', 'Services & Networking', 'Service Without Selector', 'mcq');
VALUES ('a5b1e851-27ea-4379-96d1-816715fa042d', 'a6b3cfd2-dc03-4a99-b961-9015f2fb70f4', 'A selector-less Service doesn''t get an auto-managed Endpoints object; the developer must create one manually (matching the Service''s name) pointing at the actual backend IPs/ports, commonly used to front an external resource.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('6671b471-979e-445d-97b9-a7414985d999', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 4, 'A Service exposes two ports on the same backend Pods. Why is it good practice to name each port (in both the container spec and the Service spec) rather than referencing them only by number?', 'Services & Networking', 'Multi-Port Services', 'mcq');
VALUES ('6671b471-979e-445d-97b9-a7414985d999', 'c41f5e90-7484-4ad8-b194-121eff1a505c', 'Naming ports is a readability/maintainability convention, not a hard requirement — a multi-port Service works fine with only numeric ports, but named ports make the intent clearer and are referenceable by name.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('2933e12f-84f2-4d20-9c99-0658d0abd554', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 5, 'In a Service spec''s ports entry, what''s the distinction between ''port'' and ''targetPort''?', 'Services & Networking', 'Service Port Fields', 'mcq');
VALUES ('2933e12f-84f2-4d20-9c99-0658d0abd554', '2ca44d8f-38f9-4d69-a202-10ea3fddd333', '''port'' is the Service''s own listening port; ''targetPort'' is where traffic is actually sent on the backend Pod, and the two are commonly different (e.g. Service port 80 forwarding to container port 8080).', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('9e182cd7-0cf1-4320-a1b0-82f61760ada1', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 6, 'By default, what port range does Kubernetes allocate NodePort values from?', 'Services & Networking', 'NodePort Range', 'mcq');
VALUES ('9e182cd7-0cf1-4320-a1b0-82f61760ada1', 'c16ed5ba-0d39-432f-bab2-8de6f1630740', 'The default NodePort range is 30000-32767 (configurable cluster-wide via the API server''s --service-node-port-range flag).', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('d65c4622-8a48-4bf1-9c7d-3b07c5646a2a', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 7, 'Setting a Service''s sessionAffinity to ClientIP does what?', 'Services & Networking', 'sessionAffinity', 'mcq');
VALUES ('d65c4622-8a48-4bf1-9c7d-3b07c5646a2a', '539dba0f-61cc-42cd-8276-73627b8d2c47', 'sessionAffinity: ClientIP makes kube-proxy stick a given source IP to the same backend Pod for a configurable timeout, rather than distributing every request independently.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('3e8a39b7-ddf6-4a15-8751-e713f0d13294', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 8, 'A Pod''s labels correctly match a Service''s selector, but the Pod is failing its readinessProbe. What''s the effect on that Service?', 'Services & Networking', 'Readiness and Service Endpoints', 'mcq');
VALUES ('3e8a39b7-ddf6-4a15-8751-e713f0d13294', '8caf87e2-61d2-4746-bf04-54cdba1befe8', 'Endpoints/EndpointSlice membership depends on both label match AND readiness — a Pod that matches the selector but fails readiness is removed from the routable set until it becomes Ready again.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('76905617-c18c-49bb-8c7c-79ea2745d12e', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 9, 'Running ''kubectl expose deployment my-app --port=80 --target-port=8080'' creates what?', 'Services & Networking', 'kubectl expose', 'mcq');
VALUES ('76905617-c18c-49bb-8c7c-79ea2745d12e', '135414fb-f3c7-4ef3-bdda-5726736d976e', 'kubectl expose generates a Service (ClusterIP unless --type is given) whose selector matches the source Deployment''s Pod labels, forwarding the given port to targetPort on those Pods.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('55774a58-79b7-4339-82cb-b63b702782c3', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 10, 'Kubernetes injects Service-discovery environment variables (like MY_SVC_SERVICE_HOST) into Pods, in addition to DNS. What''s the well-known limitation of relying on these env vars for service discovery, from an application-developer''s perspective?', 'Services & Networking', 'Legacy Service Discovery via Env Vars', 'mcq');
VALUES ('55774a58-79b7-4339-82cb-b63b702782c3', '423f89a9-c333-4a72-9521-0d0ae291453f', 'Service env vars are injected only at Pod creation time based on Services that existed then — this ordering limitation is exactly why DNS-based discovery is generally preferred by application developers.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('40cec85e-7fb5-4577-81d2-d7717be2cc47', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 11, 'As an app developer, what does ''kubectl port-forward svc/my-service 8080:80'' let you do?', 'Services & Networking', 'kubectl port-forward', 'mcq');
VALUES ('40cec85e-7fb5-4577-81d2-d7717be2cc47', 'a093f05c-cc70-4cf0-a88c-d28acd9d8d33', 'port-forward opens a temporary tunnel from a local port to a Service/Pod''s port for the current session only — it doesn''t modify the Service or expose it to anything outside that tunnel.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('6b697a48-f160-4224-a1f0-18cf7b61e27f', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 12, 'What does the EndpointSlice API provide as the modern, stable successor to the original Endpoints object?', 'Services & Networking', 'EndpointSlice', 'mcq');
VALUES ('6b697a48-f160-4224-a1f0-18cf7b61e27f', '47bf74c2-bfa2-41c6-a8a9-af451e118967', 'EndpointSlice (stable since Kubernetes v1.21) improves on the single, unbounded Endpoints object by sharding large backend sets across multiple slices and supporting dual-stack IPs and topology hints.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('bd3f072c-139f-4818-95d3-bfff34e3315c', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 13, 'For a Service to route traffic to a set of Pods at all, what must be true, at minimum?', 'Services & Networking', 'Service Selector Labels', 'mcq');
VALUES ('bd3f072c-139f-4818-95d3-bfff34e3315c', 'd5f09132-f41f-4b44-b974-9fedeffbbd6f', 'Service-to-Pod routing is purely label-based via spec.selector; the Service has no awareness of what controller (or none) created the matching Pods.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

-- ── Section: Ingress (10 questions) — Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum's Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material. ──

VALUES ('8652306d-f174-411b-abd6-748b117947e7', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 14, 'A single Ingress resource defines rules for host: api.example.com and host: app.example.com, each routing to different Services. What does this express?', 'Services & Networking', 'Ingress Host-Based Routing', 'mcq');
VALUES ('8652306d-f174-411b-abd6-748b117947e7', 'e7243877-ced4-48dc-a7d6-7555fe3bc3f3', 'An Ingress resource can list multiple host rules, each with its own routing, all served through the same Ingress controller and typically the same external IP/load balancer.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('376698cd-9fad-48ba-8517-9121ba3c9ed0', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 15, 'An Ingress rule sets path: /api with pathType: Prefix. What does pathType: Prefix mean here, as distinct from Exact?', 'Services & Networking', 'Ingress Path-Based Routing & pathType', 'mcq');
VALUES ('376698cd-9fad-48ba-8517-9121ba3c9ed0', '5618c9ff-028e-42b2-ad60-4448df496f20', 'pathType: Prefix does element-wise prefix matching on path segments (so /api matches /api/users), while Exact requires the request path to match the given path string exactly.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('af6c1659-c3bd-4b35-a9d4-1801de01df80', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 16, 'A request arrives at the Ingress controller that doesn''t match any rule''s host/path in any Ingress resource. What typically handles it, if configured?', 'Services & Networking', 'Ingress Default Backend', 'mcq');
VALUES ('af6c1659-c3bd-4b35-a9d4-1801de01df80', 'f18a75ad-da44-46dc-b4d0-42110b6b1ae9', 'A defaultBackend (either configured on the Ingress controller itself or via an Ingress''s spec.defaultBackend) catches requests that don''t match any defined rule.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('957a9dae-81a4-4850-ba21-7f513144663e', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 17, 'How does an Ingress resource terminate TLS for a given host?', 'Services & Networking', 'Ingress TLS', 'mcq');
VALUES ('957a9dae-81a4-4850-ba21-7f513144663e', '84433cc5-3300-4c52-bbe4-78fe191a6df4', 'TLS termination at the Ingress layer is configured via spec.tls, referencing a kubernetes.io/tls Secret holding the certificate/key the controller presents for that host.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('71be5704-485a-4354-9e1a-b9f95bcf96fe', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 18, 'A cluster has two different Ingress controllers installed. How does an Ingress resource specify which controller should handle it?', 'Services & Networking', 'ingressClassName', 'mcq');
VALUES ('71be5704-485a-4354-9e1a-b9f95bcf96fe', '12e1a0b5-37c3-4af1-b602-73939d87b435', 'spec.ingressClassName points at an IngressClass resource, which in turn identifies the controller responsible for implementing that Ingress''s rules — this is how multiple controllers coexist cleanly.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('6a97e2c3-1b46-4a9e-83ef-e750f8ac2a62', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 19, 'You create Ingress resources in a cluster where no Ingress controller has been installed. What happens?', 'Services & Networking', 'Ingress Requires a Controller', 'mcq');
VALUES ('6a97e2c3-1b46-4a9e-83ef-e750f8ac2a62', 'a3d04c3a-9e54-43d2-9fb4-cbc224d1b66c', 'Ingress is just an API object describing desired routing; it has zero effect without a running controller watching and implementing those rules.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('ee4f453d-ea78-4758-856e-0fae93565c3f', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 20, 'From an application developer''s perspective, why would you use an Ingress in front of a Service rather than just making the Service a LoadBalancer directly?', 'Services & Networking', 'Ingress vs Service', 'mcq');
VALUES ('ee4f453d-ea78-4758-856e-0fae93565c3f', '02f8eef4-fec8-434c-b55f-c73de728c487', 'Ingress''s main value is consolidating routing (and often TLS) for many backend Services behind one external endpoint, avoiding a dedicated cloud load balancer per Service.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('314ae594-c13d-44da-8d30-4d126589d19d', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 21, 'Ingress controllers commonly support behavior (like URL rewriting, e.g. nginx.ingress.kubernetes.io/rewrite-target) through which mechanism, since it''s not part of the core Ingress API spec?', 'Services & Networking', 'Ingress Annotations', 'mcq');
VALUES ('314ae594-c13d-44da-8d30-4d126589d19d', '4a68b72e-8312-448a-8cac-dd751f20b7c3', 'Behavior beyond the core Ingress spec (host/path/TLS routing) is typically exposed via controller-specific annotations, which don''t transfer if you switch Ingress controllers.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('7fba88a9-2ef8-4c0b-bcca-bf8bc3e1adb7', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 22, 'Two separate Ingress resources both define the exact same host and path, pointing to different backend Services. What can you generally expect?', 'Services & Networking', 'Same Host+Path in Two Ingress Resources', 'mcq');
VALUES ('7fba88a9-2ef8-4c0b-bcca-bf8bc3e1adb7', 'a2193266-fea9-4ff3-941c-e2da6444ecf1', 'The core Ingress API doesn''t define a merge/conflict-resolution rule for overlapping host+path across resources; behavior is left to the specific controller''s implementation, so it should be treated as a misconfiguration.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('851d0d38-480f-4b4a-9c2c-1a7bc00e8e0b', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 23, 'Does creating an Ingress resource, by itself, expose your application outside the cluster?', 'Services & Networking', 'Ingress Resource Scope', 'mcq');
VALUES ('851d0d38-480f-4b4a-9c2c-1a7bc00e8e0b', 'f44a4387-4012-4bd4-9911-fdc7d22e41bf', 'An Ingress object is declarative-only; actual external exposure comes from the controller implementing it, which is itself typically fronted by its own Service.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

-- ── Section: NetworkPolicy, DNS & Pod-to-Pod Networking (14 questions) — Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum's Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material. ──

VALUES ('e9c59080-5f05-43f6-a8c9-906038e7ff20', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 24, 'A NetworkPolicy''s spec includes only an ''egress'' block and no ''ingress'' block, but doesn''t explicitly set policyTypes. What''s the risk of omitting policyTypes here?', 'Services & Networking', 'NetworkPolicy policyTypes', 'mcq');
VALUES ('e9c59080-5f05-43f6-a8c9-906038e7ff20', '832d6a68-c054-4b15-9f3b-91eb8c13258f', 'policyTypes is inferred from which blocks are present if omitted, but this inference can silently miss your intent (e.g. wanting an ingress-only or egress-only policy) — explicit is safer.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('5900dc70-e941-4acf-b6fa-292dfec375aa', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 25, 'As an application developer packaging a NetworkPolicy alongside your own microservice''s manifests, you want to allow only Pods belonging to your own application (label app: checkout) to receive traffic from Pods labeled app: frontend, in the same namespace. Which field expresses the ''who is allowed in'' condition?', 'Services & Networking', 'App-Scoped NetworkPolicy', 'mcq');
VALUES ('5900dc70-e941-4acf-b6fa-292dfec375aa', '9cd1b7b2-d1ae-4c75-9610-4a6b4cc75eac', 'The policy''s own spec.podSelector picks which Pods it protects (app: checkout); its ingress[].from[].podSelector picks which source Pods are allowed in (app: frontend).', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('516461c6-81ff-47e6-a6fa-91d0c5c6c09d', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 26, 'You want a NetworkPolicy that restricts only outbound (egress) traffic from your Pods, while leaving inbound traffic completely unaffected by this policy. What must you make sure of?', 'Services & Networking', 'NetworkPolicy Egress-Only Restriction', 'mcq');
VALUES ('516461c6-81ff-47e6-a6fa-91d0c5c6c09d', '83862497-d770-4df1-862a-9939781d9249', 'Explicitly scoping policyTypes to [Egress] only prevents the policy from also becoming a default-deny for ingress traffic to the selected Pods.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('e22223b3-d798-4314-9abc-1c7970bc6f37', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 27, 'A NetworkPolicy''s ingress rule includes a ''ports'' field specifying protocol: TCP and port: 8080. What''s the effect?', 'Services & Networking', 'NetworkPolicy Port Restriction', 'mcq');
VALUES ('e22223b3-d798-4314-9abc-1c7970bc6f37', 'd0dee412-70ee-44e4-b1c8-7fe6b3a6f6bf', 'NetworkPolicy rules can scope allowed traffic down to specific protocol/port pairs in addition to peer selection — a rule allowing TCP/8080 doesn''t implicitly allow other ports.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('4ac926a3-aeab-47a5-ab11-36101d125498', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 28, 'You create a technically well-formed NetworkPolicy, but traffic still isn''t being restricted as expected. What''s a common root cause worth checking first?', 'Services & Networking', 'CNI Enforcement of NetworkPolicy', 'mcq');
VALUES ('4ac926a3-aeab-47a5-ab11-36101d125498', '65158623-8330-4e00-b973-d4b9ee333b77', 'NetworkPolicy is an API contract enforced by the CNI, not the control plane itself — a non-enforcing CNI silently accepts the objects without applying any restriction.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('ad0819de-460b-4b5a-ad43-40eddd59d06b', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 29, 'From inside a Pod, what''s the standard fully-qualified DNS name to reach a Service named ''payments'' in the ''billing'' namespace?', 'Services & Networking', 'Cluster DNS FQDN', 'mcq');
VALUES ('ad0819de-460b-4b5a-ad43-40eddd59d06b', '0d15fbd0-a886-43e4-9ead-8a6cbb779855', 'Cluster DNS follows <service>.<namespace>.svc.<cluster-domain>, with cluster.local as the conventional default cluster domain.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('8a6c8ff0-83ec-4d8c-9e5a-34e88273b856', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 30, 'An application in the ''frontend'' namespace wants to call a Service named ''payments'' in the ''billing'' namespace. Simply using the hostname ''payments'' will not resolve correctly from ''frontend''. Why, and what''s the fix?', 'Services & Networking', 'Cross-Namespace Service Calls', 'mcq');
VALUES ('8a6c8ff0-83ec-4d8c-9e5a-34e88273b856', '10abd6c1-5b4c-4b81-89ac-1db2be4297b1', 'The default Pod DNS search path resolves a bare name within the Pod''s own namespace first; reaching a Service in another namespace requires at least the namespace-qualified form.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('822f61cb-3fd8-464e-996c-27bf8a78a422', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 31, 'For a Pod managed by a StatefulSet behind a headless Service named ''db'', how can another Pod address one SPECIFIC ordinal Pod (not just any Pod behind the Service) by DNS name?', 'Services & Networking', 'Per-Pod DNS for StatefulSets', 'mcq');
VALUES ('822f61cb-3fd8-464e-996c-27bf8a78a422', 'ca3acbc8-0efc-4e38-98ed-9a072300bf4c', 'A headless Service backing a StatefulSet publishes individual DNS records per Pod, addressed as <pod-name>.<service-name>.<namespace>.svc.cluster.local, letting callers target one specific ordinal.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('3844b815-7b8b-4268-bebc-cb276ad7198f', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 32, 'An application needs to query a custom, non-cluster DNS nameserver instead of the cluster''s default resolution chain. Which Pod spec fields support this?', 'Services & Networking', 'Custom Pod DNS Config', 'mcq');
VALUES ('3844b815-7b8b-4268-bebc-cb276ad7198f', '465ed309-881b-4cee-848b-9a00d8b95529', 'dnsPolicy: None disables the default DNS chain entirely, requiring dnsConfig to fully specify nameservers/search domains/options for that Pod.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('4eb138dc-c06f-45d0-b22d-66e27a76e032', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 33, 'Two containers in the same Pod both want to talk to each other. What''s true about how they can reach one another?', 'Services & Networking', 'Multi-Container Pod Networking', 'mcq');
VALUES ('4eb138dc-c06f-45d0-b22d-66e27a76e032', '886de66e-3a04-4412-b9ca-1ad329035d2a', 'All containers in a Pod share one network namespace and Pod IP; they communicate over localhost without needing a Service, DNS, or any cluster networking layer.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('0e489542-2a3a-4ccf-983b-9f539dd02e9f', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 34, 'Two containers within the same Pod both try to configure their process to listen on TCP port 8080. What happens?', 'Services & Networking', 'Port Conflicts Within a Pod', 'mcq');
VALUES ('0e489542-2a3a-4ccf-983b-9f539dd02e9f', '3795e227-f693-4ef7-b889-3df9f90622e5', 'Because containers in a Pod share the network namespace, port binding is a genuine shared resource — two containers cannot both successfully bind the same port.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('456acb9b-abd8-4221-bb1e-b527f0801871', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 35, 'A sidecar container in a Pod (e.g. a log shipper or proxy) needs to reach the main application container running on port 8080 in the same Pod. What''s the standard way to do this?', 'Services & Networking', 'Sidecar-to-Main-Container Networking', 'mcq');
VALUES ('456acb9b-abd8-4221-bb1e-b527f0801871', 'c1d7782d-ee50-44d9-8c3c-3e9447acaf59', 'Same-Pod containers always reach each other over localhost — no Service, DNS entry, or external routing is involved for intra-Pod communication.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('951271b2-0d68-4403-99f8-d2aafdb0bdae', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 36, 'You''re deploying a new microservice into a namespace that already enforces default-deny NetworkPolicies for ingress. As the application''s developer, what do you need to add for your own Service to actually receive traffic from its intended callers?', 'Services & Networking', 'NetworkPolicy Default Namespace Behavior (App-Dev Angle)', 'mcq');
VALUES ('951271b2-0d68-4403-99f8-d2aafdb0bdae', '76c4d417-82e0-478c-800b-02ecd7c1a084', 'Under a default-deny-ingress posture, every workload must ship its own allow-list NetworkPolicy; there''s no per-Service opt-out, and Service type has no bearing on NetworkPolicy enforcement.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('1e0bd32a-69d2-4ce0-91f6-f4fa532cc888', '8aa25383-4b15-48b6-beb3-0f8fc7661124', 37, 'Your application Pod can reach other Pods by IP but fails to resolve any Service by name. From your own Pod''s manifest/config, what''s a quick first thing to verify before escalating to a cluster-wide CoreDNS issue?', 'Services & Networking', 'DNS Resolution Failure First Check (App-Dev Angle)', 'mcq');
VALUES ('1e0bd32a-69d2-4ce0-91f6-f4fa532cc888', '77b6bac6-0f75-452f-88ba-1ca1d928bbd7', 'A per-Pod dnsPolicy override (or a broken custom dnsConfig) is a self-contained, Pod-manifest-level cause that''s worth ruling out before assuming a cluster-wide CoreDNS failure.', 'Services & Networking — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Services, Ingress, Network Policies, DNS for Services and Pods) and the current CNCF CKAD exam curriculum''s Services & Networking domain, framed from the application-developer perspective the CKAD blueprint uses; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');
